WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.830
Today's chemical is ethanol, also called ethyl alcohol, CAS number 64-17-5.

00:00:06.830 --> 00:00:11.910
Ethanol is highly flammable, with a flash point of about 13 degrees Celsius.

00:00:11.910 --> 00:00:15.150
Its heavy vapor can travel to a spark and flash back.

00:00:15.150 --> 00:00:19.210
It irritates the eyes and airways and can make you drowsy or dizzy.

00:00:19.210 --> 00:00:25.700
This MSDS also lists cancer, genetic defects, and harm to fertility or an unborn child.

00:00:25.700 --> 00:00:31.440
This evidence comes mainly from drinking alcohol, but keep exposure low to protect your organs.

00:00:31.440 --> 00:00:37.030
Keep away from heat and sparks, ground equipment, and never eat, drink or smoke while handling.

00:00:37.030 --> 00:00:40.130
Store it sealed in a cool, ventilated, locked area.

00:00:40.130 --> 00:00:45.780
Wear gloves, safety goggles and protective clothing, plus a gas mask when exposure is high.

00:00:45.780 --> 00:00:49.430
Eyes: rinse carefully with water and remove contact lenses.

00:00:49.430 --> 00:00:53.110
Skin: wash with soap and water. Inhaled: get fresh air.

00:00:53.110 --> 00:00:56.890
Spill: remove ignition sources and absorb with dry sand.

00:00:56.890 --> 00:01:00.410
Fire: use alcohol foam, CO2 or water spray.

00:01:00.410 --> 00:01:05.980
On the label, pictograms show the hazard type. The signal word Danger means serious risk.

00:01:05.980 --> 00:01:10.780
Hazard statements explain the risk; precautionary statements tell you what to do.

00:01:10.780 --> 00:01:15.820
The full MSDS has 16 sections. Check it at your workplace before handling.
